# Session files written by the running app.
#
# The 16 real pilot sessions (dated 2026-07-31) are already tracked, and
# .gitignore does not affect tracked files — so they stay in git and changes to
# them still show. This only stops NEW ones being committed.
#
# It matters because analyze_sessions.py counts every file in sessions/ as
# participant data. Six artefacts from container testing were committed during
# Phase 0 and inflated the reported dataset from 16 to 22.
sessions/*.json
